# Area template

Part of the [[README]]. Skeleton for a new Area in `Areas/`. Creating an Area is reported prominently ([[agent-protocol]]). Rules: [[organization]], [[schema]], [[body-sections]].

**Using it:** [[= owner =]] creates a new file in `Areas/`, and Templater fills it. Agents copy it by hand and save it as `Areas/<slug>.md`. Both, in detail: [[template-task]]. Then:

- Replace the first body line with the standard being maintained.
- Add `people:` and `resources:` only for a curated few key People and Resources. Never a `projects:` field; the Projects block lists them.
- Delete the Someday/maybe and Notes headings if empty.

<%*
tR = "";
let title = tp.file.title;
if (title.startsWith("Untitled")) title = await tp.system.prompt("Area title (sentence case)");
const slug = title.normalize("NFKD").replace(/[^\x00-\x7F]/g, "").toLowerCase().replace(/'/g, "").replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "");
await tp.file.move("Areas/" + slug);
-%>
